{
 "encounter_id": "00822",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "NURSE"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Mr Hegarty? Hello! I'm Mairead. Roll up that sleeve and I'll do your blood pressure, and your temperature, and so on. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ah, grand, grand. I'll tell you everything while you do it. I've had this throat for months, and I'll talk about the weather, I don't mind. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Blood pressure 136 over 82, pulse 74, temperature 36.7, oxygen 98 percent, weight 80 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good morning, Mr Hegarty. It's the sore throat, isn't it? How is it now?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Still there. It's five months now, the sore throat, on and off, and sometimes it's hard to swallow, like there's a lump in it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Which side?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The right, mainly. And I've a hoarse voice, as well, since Christmas."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any pain going to your ear? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Sometimes, the right ear. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any blood in your spit, or weight loss?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No blood. No weight loss."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any lump in your neck that you've noticed?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No lump. I've felt, nothing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What tablets are you taking?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Omeprazole, 20 mg, every morning. Amlodipine, 5 mg. And a statin, simvastatin, 20 mg, at night."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any allergies?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Penicillin. I came out in a rash."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And your history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Acid reflux, high blood pressure, and high cholesterol."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you have a family history of throat or neck cancer?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My father had cancer of the voice box, he smoked eighty a day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And do you smoke or drink?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I gave it up in 2015, after the heart scare. And a few pints at the weekend."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Right. Because it's been five months, and you have a hoarse voice, I need to look properly. Let me feel your neck. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Go on.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'll get the camera ready, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thanks, Mairead. There's no lump in your neck. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's a relief. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "But the hoarseness and the sore throat for that long, in someone with a smoking history, need a proper look with a camera. I'd say this could be reflux irritating the voice box, but I can't rule out something more serious, like a growth."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Cancer? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I don't think so, but I must be sure. I'd like to refer you urgently to the ENT clinic, to have a camera passed through your nose to see your voice box."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "When? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Within two weeks. They'll write. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "In the meantime, keep taking the omeprazole, avoid late meals, alcohol and spicy food, and don't clear your throat or whisper."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd also like a chest X-ray, as a precaution, because of your smoking history."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks, once ENT have seen you."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three weeks. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
